#compdef openclaw
# Lazy loader for the openclaw CLI completion.
#
# The installer writes ~/.openclaw/completions/openclaw.zsh (201 KB, 5,406
# lines) and tells you to `source` it from .zshrc. That parsed the whole file on
# every interactive shell start, measured at 5.0 ms, to define a completion
# almost no shell ever uses. This file is autoloaded by compinit instead, so the
# cost moves to the first Tab after `openclaw `.
#
# Sourcing the vendor file rather than copying it means an `openclaw update`
# is picked up with no regeneration step here. The vendor file defines
# _openclaw_root_completion, not _openclaw, so this redefines itself to
# delegate; the source therefore runs once per shell, not once per Tab.
#
# Lives in ~/.zfunc, on fpath via the fpath=() block in ~/.zshenv.

[[ -r "$HOME/.openclaw/completions/openclaw.zsh" ]] || return 1
source "$HOME/.openclaw/completions/openclaw.zsh"
_openclaw() { _openclaw_root_completion "$@" }
_openclaw "$@"
